# HPE Search Engine — Project Analysis

## What This Project Is

An **HPE Campus Connect Program** enterprise search engine that lets users **upload files to object storage and search through them using natural language**. It's a hybrid semantic + keyword search system, built as a team project with clearly delineated roles.

---

## Architecture Overview (from Flow.png)

The system has two clearly separated stages:

```
Stage 1: Background Ingestion (async, event-driven)
Stage 2: Real-time Search (synchronous, latency-sensitive)
```

![Architecture Flow](/home/praneeth08/HPE/Search-Engine/Architecture/Flow.png)

---

## Stage 1 — Background Ingestion

| Step | Component | Role |
|------|-----------|------|
| 1 | **User** | Uploads a file |
| 2 | **MinIO** | S3-compatible object store; triggers event on upload |
| 3 | **Kafka** | Message queue; receives the MinIO event and buffers it |
| 4 | **PyWorker-1 (Indexer)** | Consumes from Kafka and runs the ingestion pipeline |
| ↳ | **Apache Tika** | Extracts raw text from PDFs, DOCX, PPTX, images, etc. |
| ↳ | **LangChain** | Chunks the extracted text (configurable size & overlap) |
| ↳ | **SentenceTransformers** | Encodes chunks → dense vectors (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`) |
| 5 | **OpenSearch** | Stores both dense kNN vectors AND BM25 keyword index in a single cluster |

> Both indexes (semantic kNN + keyword BM25) live **inside one OpenSearch cluster** — this is a key design decision that simplifies the stack by eliminating a separate Qdrant instance.

---

## Stage 2 — Real-time Search

| Step | Component | Role |
|------|-----------|------|
| 1 | **User** | Types a natural language query |
| 2 | **Go Gateway** | REST API entry point; hashes query and checks Redis |
| 3a | **Redis (hit)** | Returns cached results instantly with TTL |
| 3b | **Redis (miss)** | Triggers gRPC call to PyWorker-2 |
| 4 | **PyWorker-2 (Searcher)** | NLP parsing + embedding via gRPC |
| ↳ | **LangChain** | NLP query parse → extracts intent, keywords, filters |
| ↳ | **SentenceTransformers** | Embeds the cleaned intent text |
| 5 | **OpenSearch** | Executes hybrid kNN + BM25 query |
| 6 | **Go Backend** | Merges Top-K results from both indexes |
| 7 | **Redis** | Stores final result JSON with TTL |
| 8 | **Frontend** | Receives snippets + file URLs, renders them |

